{"traceId":"ce11a089f3a0cb6c8c4d61635e07ee43","spans":{"99243096a2740eca":{"spanId":"99243096a2740eca","traceId":"ce11a089f3a0cb6c8c4d61635e07ee43","parentSpanId":"0124e1be8be3fc59","startTime":1753401274005,"endTime":1753401292710.7568,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/o3","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/o3,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"You are a member of the Partagaz D analysis group, a software development expert with a focus on quality, safety, and QA best-practices.\\n\\nYou will be given a \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\", or DEP. This is a document from a development firm outlining a plan of development for a software product.\\n\\nYou will also be given the user's initial goals & messages.\\n\\nYour goal is to APPROVE or DENY this DEP based on your own judgement and these guidance questions:\\n\\n-> Does the DEP fulfill ALL of the user's requirements? Would they be satisfied with the product outlined in the DEP?\\n-> Is the DEP as deterministic as possible? Small needed user inputs (project name, API keys, etc.) are OK but are any code files missing?\\n-> Is the DEP quality? Is it safe? There is no need for every DEP to be a \\\"F1 race car\\\", but even \\\"sedan\\\"-level products (simple websites) should be safe and secure.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"A new Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) has been submitted for review. Please analyze the following DEP and respond with only \\\"APPROVE\\\" if you approve it, or \\\"DENY\\\" followed by your reasoning if you deny it.\\n\\n---BEGIN USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\nQuestion: Hello! I’m Delta, your Chief of Staff. What top priorities, tasks, or projects would you like me to focus on first so I can begin organizing the right support for you?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 1) Approximate monthly/annual budget you’re comfortable with for hosting and related services?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 2) How would you like residents to receive login credentials? (Self-register with approval, admin-created accounts, invite-only links, etc.)\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 3) Do you already own a domain name, or will you need assistance purchasing/setting one up?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 4) Roughly how many households/residents need access today, and do you expect significant growth?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 5) For news & updates, would you prefer a simple text editor built into the site (similar to writing an email) so you can add posts yourself without code?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 6) Do you have existing logo, color scheme, or any branding guidelines we should incorporate?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 1) To keep costs well under $50/month and give you a familiar text-editor experience, may I proceed with WordPress hosted on AWS Lightsail (~$5 per month, including SSL)?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 2) The seasonal theme idea: would simple color-scheme changes (winter blues, fall oranges, etc.) that switch automatically each season meet your vision, or do you prefer full background images/graphics as well?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 3) Which email address should incoming messages from the site’s “Contact Us” form be sent to?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\n---END USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\n\\n---BEGIN DEP---\\nDETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP) — Dunbar Oaks HOA Website\\n\\n=== 0. Prerequisites ===\\n• AWS account with billing enabled (root-level or IAM user with Lightsail + Route 53 permissions).\\n• Access to dunbaroakshoa.com domain registrar control panel (to update A/CNAME records).\\n\\n=== 1. Infrastructure Provisioning ===\\n1.1  CLI/Console: Create AWS Lightsail instance:\\n     • Blueprint: WordPress Multisite (Bitnami) or single-site (choose single-site).\\n     • Plan: 1 vCPU / 1 GB RAM / 40 GB SSD (~US $5 mo).\\n     • Region: us-east-1 (or closest to HOA).\\n     • Instance name: dunbaroakshoa-wp.\\n1.2  Allocate & attach a static IP to the instance (Name: dunbaroakshoa-static-ip).\\n1.3  Enable Lightsail automatic daily snapshot backup ($0.05/GB-mo after 7 days retention cap— fits budget).\\n1.4  Open networking ports: 80 (HTTP), 443 (HTTPS), 22 (SSH). Remove all others.\\n\\n=== 2. Domain & SSL ===\\n2.1  In domain registrar DNS panel, create:\\n     • A record @ -> <STATIC_IP>\\n     • CNAME www -> @\\n2.2  SSH into instance → run sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool and request Let’s Encrypt certificate for:\\n        dunbaroakshoa.com, www.dunbaroakshoa.com\\n     Accept redirect HTTP→HTTPS and set auto-renewal.\\n\\n=== 3. WordPress Core Setup ===\\n3.1  Retrieve initial WP password:\\n        cat ~/bitnami_application_password\\n3.2  Log in at https://dunbaroakshoa.com/wp-admin using user “user”.\\n3.3  Immediately create NEW admin account (username: hoaboard) with strong password; email to board@dunbaroakshoa.com. Log out and log back in as hoaboard. Delete default “user” account.\\n3.4  Set Site Title: “Dunbar Oaks HOA”. Tagline: “Community & Updates”.\\n\\n=== 4. Essential Plugins ===\\nInstall & activate (Plugins → Add New):\\n  • Members (memberpress.com/members – free)  OR “WP Members” by RocketGeek (supports manual approval).\\n  • WPForms Lite (contact form).\\n  • Restrict User Access (optional if Members covers page protection).\\n  • WP Crontrol (schedule seasonal color switch).\\n  • Code Snippet plugin (e.g., “Code Snippets”) for custom PHP/CSS injections.\\n  • (Optional) “Really Simple SSL” to enforce HTTPS (bncert already handles redirects).\\n\\n=== 5. User Registration & Protection ===\\n5.1  Members → Settings → Registration:\\n       • Enable frontend registration.\\n       • Require admin approval (email notification to board@dunbaroakshoa.com).\\n5.2  Create “Resident” role.\\n5.3  Protect pages/categories so only role=Resident see Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events.\\n\\n=== 6. Pages & Navigation ===\\nCreate pages (Pages → Add New):\\n  • Contact Us (public) – embed WPForms contact form; configure notifications to board@dunbaroakshoa.com.\\n  • Bylaws (public) – upload PDF or paste text.\\n  • Schools (public) – list nearby schools.\\n  • Dues (protected) – financial info.\\n  • Annual Meetings (protected) – meeting minutes uploads.\\n  • News & Events (protected) – posts category.\\nAdd to primary menu (Appearance → Menus) in requested order.\\n\\n=== 7. News & Updates Editing Experience ===\\n7.1  Ensure Gutenberg (block) editor active (default). User can write posts via simple text interface.\\n7.2  Optionally install “Classic Editor” if simpler UI desired.\\n\\n=== 8. Seasonal Color Theme Automation ===\\n8.1  Theme: Use default “Twenty Twenty-Four” (lightweight) + child theme.\\n8.2  Child theme style.css holds four color palettes (winter, spring, summer, fall).\\n8.3  In Code Snippets add PHP:\\n      function dohoa_season_css() {\\n        $month = (int) date('n');\\n        if (in_array($month, [12,1,2])) $season='winter';\\n        elseif (in_array($month,[3,4,5])) $season='spring';\\n        elseif (in_array($month,[6,7,8])) $season='summer';\\n        else $season='fall';\\n        wp_enqueue_style('dohoa-'.$season, get_stylesheet_directory_uri().\\\"/css/\\\".$season.\\\".css\\\", [], null);\\n      }\\n      add_action('wp_enqueue_scripts','dohoa_season_css');\\n8.4  Create /css/winter.css, spring.css, summer.css, fall.css with palette tweaks (e.g., winter blues, fall oranges).\\n(This runs automatically; WP Crontrol not strictly needed but can later add cron to flush cache monthly.)\\n\\n=== 9. Contact Form ===\\n9.1  WPForms Lite → Add New → “Contact Form”. Fields: Name, Email, Subject, Message.\\n9.2  Settings → Notifications: Send To board@dunbaroakshoa.com; subject includes {field_subject}.\\n9.3  Embed shortcode on Contact Us page.\\n\\n===10. Security Hardening ===\\n10.1  In Lightsail networking, restrict SSH to HOA board’s IP range if provided, else leave open but change SSH key.\\n10.2  Install “Wordfence Security” (free) for basic firewall & login limit.\\n10.3  Force HTTPS in wp-config.php if not already.\\n10.4  Schedule automatic WordPress & plugin updates (enable in Lightsail/Bitnami bnconfig).\\n\\n===11. Backups & Monitoring ===\\n11.1  Verify daily snapshot in Lightsail.\\n11.2  In WP Admin install “UpdraftPlus” (optional) for offsite backups to S3 bucket (can stay free tier).\\n\\n===12. Testing Checklist ===\\n☐ Public pages load over HTTPS.\\n☐ Registration form visible; registration triggers “awaiting approval” email.\\n☐ Admin approves user; protected pages visible only to logged-in approved user.\\n☐ Contact form sends email to board@.\\n☐ Seasonal color switch verified by temporarily changing system month in snippet for test.\\n\\n===13. Delivery to User ===\\nProvide URL, WP admin login, and a 1-page quick-start PDF (how to approve users, add posts, and change seasonal colors list).\\n\\n===14. Rollback / Teardown ===\\n• If major failure, restore from latest snapshot (Lightsail → Snapshots → Create New/Restore).\\n• To delete resources: detach & release static IP, delete instance, delete snapshots, update DNS.\\n\\n===15. Cost Estimate ===\\n• Lightsail plan: ~$5.00/mo.\\n• Domain: existing (no added cost).\\n• Optional S3 offsite backup: pennies (<$0.50/mo for <1 GB).\\nTOTAL ≈ $5-6 / month < user’s $50 ceiling.\\n---END DEP---\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"APPROVE\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":2143,\"outputTokens\":789,\"totalTokens\":2932},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx03fNqNuPDEWMcbyLLH8iQmSTUZz\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753401275,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"APPROV